  "notes": "v235 — NAV-MAP-BLANK-V40 CORRECTIVE (owner's recording, Fri Oct 23, 2026 10:18 MDT; follows v232 the same day). v232 capped the drive tile layer at native zoom 16 and healed fringe areas generally — but the tile-by-tile verification that followed (the shipped build, his exact state: parked at home 51.15709,-113.93862, route to Piegan Dog Park) showed his own block is STILL a beige field under v232: Esri's detailed-cache hole over his crescent reaches down through zoom 16 (z18/z17 tiles one flat colour; his z16 tile empty; the arterial one tile south drawn; his work areas — 15th Street, Piegan, the pits — rich at z16). The deepest Esri level that carries his street network is zoom 15 (verified visually: his subdivision grid + Country Hills Blvd draw at z15). THE FIX (modules/navigator.js only): maxNativeZoom 16 -> 15 on the drive tile layer; the drive view stays at zoom 18 (v178 framing), Leaflet scales the z15 tiles up — a softer raster than z16 where z16 had data, traded openly for a map that is never blank where he lives and starts every drive. Tile source unchanged (NAV-MAP-COLORS-3D owns any source/look change; still queued, as are NAV-INSET-SMALL-TOPRIGHT, NAV-LANE-INFO-REAL, NAV-LAYERS-BUTTON — none built here). REPRODUCTION-FIRST: the RED was the live probe on v232 itself (z16 tiles loaded, screenshot still a beige field over his block, palette-matched to the empty tiles); tools/nav-tile-coverage-v232-test.js updated to the z15 contract, 5/5 GREEN; the live GREEN (z15 tiles + his street grid around the truck) is in the run report. REGRESSIONS: drive-surface-v227 31/31; navigator-test 178/180 identical to HEAD (the parked NAVTEST-V128-STUB-GAP). Standing pin move 234 -> 235 across index.html and the test files. Native unchanged (v42 carries the web-OTA pointer; no new APK). Machine-green is preparation — the final verdict is his next look at the map at home and his next real drive.",
